pi-darksakana bundles two themes and two extension packs. Third-party origins:

1. Cyberdeck pack — extensions/cyberdeck/**, themes/violet-cyberdeck.json
   Forked from pi-sakura-cyberdeck by beautifulrem (MIT):
   https://github.com/beautifulrem/pi-sakura-cyberdeck
   Changes: the pink/sakura palette was replaced with a violet family
   (theme renamed sakura-macaron -> violet-cyberdeck); the anime braille
   startup art was replaced with an ANSI Shadow "PI" mark; the bundled
   dual-quota extension was removed.

   This pack includes a modified copy of pi-zentui by Luka (MIT):
   https://github.com/lmilojevicc/pi-zentui
   Full license text: licenses/pi-zentui-MIT.txt
   Changes: Violet Cyberdeck palette, truecolor gradient editor chrome,
   package-specific defaults, package-specific configuration path.

   claude-shimmer is a violet-themed fork of pi-claude-shimmer by ouzhenkun
   (MIT): https://github.com/ouzhenkun/pi-claude-shimmer

2. Dark Sakana pack — extensions/darksakana/**, themes/dark-sakana.json
   Original work for this repository. The dark-sakana theme is a renamed
   copy of Pi's built-in `dark` theme; the startup header mirrors the
   cyberdeck header extension's approach.

